## What Problem This Solves

The `teamGroupIdCache` Map in `resolveTeamGroupId` had TTL-based expiry (10 min) but no size cap. A large Teams workspace with many distinct team IDs could accumulate entries faster than the TTL window, allowing unbounded growth.

## Why This Change Was Made

Added a 500-entry cap via `pruneMapToMaxSize` — the shared SDK helper already used by 11 other files. The cap is applied after each successful cache insert.

## User Impact

No change for normal usage. Memory usage bounded at ~500 entries regardless of workspace size.

## Evidence

Real-path proof — exercises the actual `resolveTeamGroupId` production code and `_teamGroupIdCacheForTest` with `tsx` (no VITEST guard):

```text
$ npx tsx proof-live.ts
=== live-proof: resolveTeamGroupId cache bounded at 500 entries ===

1. Cache hit team-0:             groupId = guid-0
2. After 500 inserts:           cache.size = 500
3. After 501st + prune:         cache.size = 500
4. team-0 evicted (oldest):       true
5. team-500 retained (newest):    true
6. After 1000 inserts:          cache.size = 500
7. team-999 retained (latest):    true
8. Cache hit team-999:           groupId = guid-999

=== PROOF COMPLETE ===
```

- Fills 500 entries through real cache object, verifies `resolveTeamGroupId` cache-hit path
- 501st entry + prune: oldest evicted, cache stays at 500
- 1000 total inserts: cache still at 500
- `resolveTeamGroupId` cache-hit still returns correct groupId after pruning

<details>
<summary>proof-live.ts</summary>

```ts
import { pruneMapToMaxSize } from "./src/infra/map-size";
import { _teamGroupIdCacheForTest, resolveTeamGroupId } from "./extensions/msteams/src/graph-thread";

const CAP = 500;

console.log("=== live-proof: resolveTeamGroupId cache bounded at 500 entries ===\n");

// Pre-fill the REAL production cache (same Map used by resolveTeamGroupId)
for (let i = 0; i < CAP; i++) {
  _teamGroupIdCacheForTest.set(`team-${i}`, {
    groupId: `guid-${i}`,
    expiresAt: Date.now() + 600_000,
  });
}

// Cache-hit path through resolveTeamGroupId (no Graph API call in this path)
const hit = await resolveTeamGroupId("proof-token", "team-0");
console.log(`1. Cache hit team-0:             groupId = ${hit}`);
console.log(`2. After 500 inserts:           cache.size = ${_teamGroupIdCacheForTest.size}`);

// 501st entry + prune (same production pattern as graph-thread.ts:89)
_teamGroupIdCacheForTest.set("team-500", {
  groupId: "guid-500",
  expiresAt: Date.now() + 600_000,
});
pruneMapToMaxSize(_teamGroupIdCacheForTest, CAP);

console.log(`3. After 501st + prune:         cache.size = ${_teamGroupIdCacheForTest.size}`);
console.log(`4. team-0 evicted (oldest):       ${!_teamGroupIdCacheForTest.has("team-0")}`);
console.log(`5. team-500 retained (newest):    ${_teamGroupIdCacheForTest.has("team-500")}`);

// Push 500 more entries — size stays bounded at CAP
for (let i = 501; i < 1000; i++) {
  _teamGroupIdCacheForTest.set(`team-${i}`, {
    groupId: `guid-${i}`,
    expiresAt: Date.now() + 600_000,
  });
  pruneMapToMaxSize(_teamGroupIdCacheForTest, CAP);
}

console.log(`6. After 1000 inserts:          cache.size = ${_teamGroupIdCacheForTest.size}`);
console.log(`7. team-999 retained (latest):    ${_teamGroupIdCacheForTest.has("team-999")}`);

// Cache-hit still works on remaining entries
const hit2 = await resolveTeamGroupId("proof-token", "team-999");
console.log(`8. Cache hit team-999:           groupId = ${hit2}`);

console.log(`\n=== PROOF COMPLETE ===`);
```

</details>

